1
00:00:42,245 --> 00:00:45,185
I used to think the world was being exceptionally cruel to me.

2
00:00:53,155 --> 00:00:54,355
I was resentful...

3
00:00:56,455 --> 00:00:57,795
and filled with blame.

4
00:01:01,595 --> 00:01:03,035
Even as time passed,

5
00:01:03,665 --> 00:01:05,865
the wound didn't heal easily.

6
00:01:06,835 --> 00:01:07,835
Mi Young.

7
00:01:11,035 --> 00:01:12,275
I have really missed you.

8
00:01:13,845 --> 00:01:14,875
Look,

9
00:01:15,815 --> 00:01:17,745
from now on, just pretend you don't know me.

10
00:01:19,215 --> 00:01:20,315
To me,

11
00:01:21,485 --> 00:01:23,715
you are like someone who doesn't exist.

12
00:01:25,785 --> 00:01:27,555
The entire family was caught up...

13
00:01:28,355 --> 00:01:30,525
in a soap opera of epic proportions.

14
00:01:32,095 --> 00:01:34,695
But within that wound...

15
00:01:37,835 --> 00:01:39,935
lay a secret I knew nothing about.

16
00:01:42,805 --> 00:01:43,835
How...

17
00:01:46,905 --> 00:01:48,145
How could you?

18
00:01:50,675 --> 00:01:51,715
Mi Young.

19
00:01:52,985 --> 00:01:53,985
All this time...

20
00:01:55,455 --> 00:01:57,855
All this time, I hated you so much.

21
00:01:58,655 --> 00:02:00,425
So does that mean this wound...

22
00:02:02,025 --> 00:02:03,525
(CEO Baek Mi Young)

23
00:02:03,595 --> 00:02:05,525
isn't a wound anymore?

24
00:02:07,965 --> 00:02:09,535
(Calvin)

25
00:02:12,365 --> 00:02:13,765
Yes. It's me.

26
00:02:17,205 --> 00:02:19,475
Now, I can't be sure of anything.

27
00:02:20,245 --> 00:02:21,945
(Untitled)

28
00:02:22,015 --> 00:02:23,315
Not even...

29
00:02:25,885 --> 00:02:27,185
my own heart.

30
00:02:29,615 --> 00:02:31,155
(Episode 5)

31
00:03:00,015 --> 00:03:02,385
No way. Are you working?

32
00:03:02,815 --> 00:03:05,185
What about you? Don't you have plans on your day off?

33
00:03:05,825 --> 00:03:08,595
No, my tennis club is just nearby.

34
00:03:09,525 --> 00:03:11,695
I was passing by and saw the door was open, so I thought I'd stop in.

35
00:03:12,495 --> 00:03:14,695
But seriously, do you ever do anything but work?

36
00:03:15,495 --> 00:03:16,935
Come on, let's just go bowling.

37
00:03:20,535 --> 00:03:21,535
Kyung Tae.

38
00:03:24,505 --> 00:03:27,045
Let's say someone completely stabbed you in the back.

39
00:03:28,045 --> 00:03:29,045
What would you do?

40
00:03:29,645 --> 00:03:30,915
Stabbed in the back?

41
00:03:34,585 --> 00:03:37,715
Well, I'd have to do the same thing to them, wouldn't I?

42
00:03:53,335 --> 00:03:54,505
This is perfect.

43
00:03:54,905 --> 00:03:55,975
Are you that happy?

44
00:03:56,405 --> 00:03:57,435
Of course.

45
00:03:57,975 --> 00:04:00,145
I've been working for days to get this.

46
00:04:01,205 --> 00:04:02,345
Anyway, thank you...

47
00:04:02,615 --> 00:04:03,745
for your cooperation.

48
00:04:11,455 --> 00:04:12,655
The painting's a little abstract, isn't it?

49
00:04:14,985 --> 00:04:17,095
No matter how much I look at it, I don't really get it.

50
00:04:18,525 --> 00:04:21,265
- What about you? - I understood it at a glance.

51
00:04:21,465 --> 00:04:22,495
Oh, really?

52
00:04:24,565 --> 00:04:27,465
They sure didn't skimp on the paint.

53
00:04:27,665 --> 00:04:28,975
And they used good brushes, too.

54
00:04:30,205 --> 00:04:31,205
What?

55
00:04:33,005 --> 00:04:34,005
I know, right?

56
00:04:34,775 --> 00:04:36,075
Look over there.

57
00:04:36,815 --> 00:04:40,045
- Gosh, he's gorgeous. - He's so handsome.

58
00:04:40,115 --> 00:04:41,215
He's coming this way.

59
00:04:54,095 --> 00:04:55,165
What did you think of the exhibit?

60
00:04:55,565 --> 00:04:57,595
It was interesting. I enjoyed it.

61
00:04:59,105 --> 00:05:01,635
Thanks. It's been a while since I've been to a place like this.

62
00:05:02,075 --> 00:05:03,075
Don't thank me.

63
00:05:03,605 --> 00:05:06,075
I should be thanking you for coming with me.

64
00:05:15,515 --> 00:05:16,515
You're still the same.

65
00:05:18,785 --> 00:05:21,285
Your face when you smile hasn't changed a bit.

66
00:05:22,295 --> 00:05:23,655
You're exactly the same as you were in college.

67
00:05:25,895 --> 00:05:28,125
Please. I'm so old now.

68
00:05:28,565 --> 00:05:29,835
What do you mean, old?

69
00:05:30,235 --> 00:05:32,305
People will hate you if you say things like that.

70
00:05:32,435 --> 00:05:34,035
No, stop it.

71
00:05:34,335 --> 00:05:35,935
What? But it's true.

72
00:05:36,805 --> 00:05:38,975
Fine, should I ask the people here?

73
00:05:40,275 --> 00:05:41,275
Excuse me.

74
00:05:41,845 --> 00:05:42,845
All right.

75
00:05:43,745 --> 00:05:44,745
I'm not old.

76
00:05:47,645 --> 00:05:48,645
That's better.

77
00:05:50,415 --> 00:05:52,925
It's good to see you smile.

78
00:05:58,095 --> 00:05:59,095
So...

79
00:05:59,965 --> 00:06:02,735
Do you have a little more time?

80
00:06:05,905 --> 00:06:07,765
There's a place I'd like to go with you.

81
00:06:16,775 --> 00:06:18,615
This place hasn't changed at all.

82
00:06:22,015 --> 00:06:24,455
Oh, this sofa is the same too.

83
00:06:25,725 --> 00:06:28,825
This spot right here used to be our spot.

84
00:06:33,925 --> 00:06:35,225
Oh, here it is.

85
00:06:37,895 --> 00:06:38,905
Remember?

86
00:06:39,305 --> 00:06:40,905
We said we would read this whole series in one day,

87
00:06:41,405 --> 00:06:42,975
and we even stayed up all night here together.

88
00:06:45,875 --> 00:06:48,175
We both loved them back then.

89
00:06:51,915 --> 00:06:52,915
Comic books.

90
00:06:55,785 --> 00:06:57,885
So, what should we read today?

91
00:07:08,265 --> 00:07:09,295
You want to read this one?

92
00:07:09,865 --> 00:07:10,865
Here.

93
00:07:16,975 --> 00:07:17,975
A debt?

94
00:07:18,235 --> 00:07:19,675
Last time, my mom...

95
00:07:20,445 --> 00:07:21,445
took a lot from you.

96
00:07:21,505 --> 00:07:23,045
- Mom. - That woman...

97
00:07:23,045 --> 00:07:26,315
- What are you doing? - Oh, that?

98
00:07:26,845 --> 00:07:27,885
It's fine.

99
00:07:28,815 --> 00:07:30,915
I took plenty for myself too.

100
00:07:30,985 --> 00:07:32,485
Oh, so you did.

101
00:07:33,625 --> 00:07:35,025
So, do you always do this kind of investigating...

102
00:07:35,085 --> 00:07:36,095
to catch an affair?

103
00:07:36,755 --> 00:07:38,325
Of course.

104
00:07:39,165 --> 00:07:41,525
You may be called a lawyer, but this is just grunt work.

105
00:07:41,925 --> 00:07:45,065
I thought people in professions like yours had it pretty easy.

106
00:07:45,465 --> 00:07:47,335
It used to be a little easier.

107
00:07:48,705 --> 00:07:51,035
But then I got tangled up with an imoogi a year ago.

108
00:07:52,305 --> 00:07:55,715
Now, I'm just pounding the pavement without an office.

109
00:07:56,245 --> 00:07:57,245
An imoogi?

110
00:07:57,875 --> 00:07:58,885
There is one.

111
00:08:00,085 --> 00:08:03,085
A two-hundred-year-old imoogi who lives in Sinwol-dong.

112
00:08:09,425 --> 00:08:10,455
Here.

113
00:08:10,695 --> 00:08:13,695
Anyway, it must be tough without an office.

114
00:08:14,795 --> 00:08:17,795
Well, you couldn't be a lawyer if it was all hardship.

115
00:08:18,565 --> 00:08:20,605
When you work hard and win a case,

116
00:08:21,505 --> 00:08:22,505
the payoff is pretty good.

117
00:08:22,605 --> 00:08:25,035
Oh, right. So the money's good.

118
00:08:32,445 --> 00:08:33,785
Yes. This is Jeon Chi Hyun.

119
00:08:34,185 --> 00:08:37,255
I'm the attorney representing Mr. Ji Won Ho.

120
00:08:37,755 --> 00:08:40,225
- Oh, yes. - I've sent the written response.

121
00:08:40,285 --> 00:08:42,155
You can check it via the electronic filing system.

122
00:08:42,925 --> 00:08:43,925
That is all.

123
00:08:44,295 --> 00:08:45,355
What was that?

124
00:08:45,995 --> 00:08:47,765
What's his problem?

125
00:08:47,825 --> 00:08:49,595
(Response Defendant: Ji Won Ho Legal Rep.: Attorney Bae Su Ji)

126
00:08:49,765 --> 00:08:51,065
"Divorce petition..."

127
00:08:52,905 --> 00:08:55,205
(Legal Representative: Attorney Bae Su Ji)

128
00:08:56,305 --> 00:08:57,705
Oh my, shit!

129
00:09:06,915 --> 00:09:10,155
It's been so long since I've walked with you like this.

130
00:09:12,285 --> 00:09:13,285
I know.

131
00:09:14,185 --> 00:09:16,195
I never thought a day like this would come again.

132
00:09:18,095 --> 00:09:19,125
This is so nice.

133
00:09:21,725 --> 00:09:22,765
Let's...

134
00:09:25,735 --> 00:09:28,305
I hope we can just stay like this.

135
00:09:29,635 --> 00:09:31,275
Working together comfortably...

136
00:09:32,945 --> 00:09:35,205
and talking over tea sometimes.

137
00:09:37,075 --> 00:09:38,075
Okay.

138
00:09:38,745 --> 00:09:40,015
I won't ask for more.

139
00:09:41,185 --> 00:09:42,185
And...

140
00:09:47,225 --> 00:09:48,325
I'm getting divorced soon.

141
00:09:50,595 --> 00:09:51,625
Mi Young.

142
00:09:51,925 --> 00:09:54,025
The reason I'm telling you this...

143
00:09:55,665 --> 00:09:59,105
is to make it clear that regardless of my situation,

144
00:10:00,065 --> 00:10:01,705
there can't be anything more between us.

145
00:10:06,975 --> 00:10:07,975
One moment.

146
00:10:11,145 --> 00:10:12,215
Yes, Ms. Jeon.

147
00:10:12,545 --> 00:10:14,585
I just received their written response.

148
00:10:14,985 --> 00:10:17,155
- Yes. - Regarding the response,

149
00:10:17,315 --> 00:10:19,655
I'll text you a screenshot, so please check it right away.

150
00:10:20,055 --> 00:10:21,085
Okay, I will.

151
00:10:22,855 --> 00:10:23,895
(Response to Claims, Divorce, Alimony, Assets)

152
00:10:23,955 --> 00:10:24,955
(The defendant states they have no intention of divorcing.)

153
00:10:27,295 --> 00:10:30,535
(The defendant states they have no intention of divorcing.)

154
00:10:43,175 --> 00:10:44,175
What is this?

155
00:10:45,115 --> 00:10:47,515
- It's the written response. - I'm asking what this means.

156
00:10:47,985 --> 00:10:49,985
Why are you suddenly refusing to get a divorce?

157
00:10:50,055 --> 00:10:51,415
What's with the change of heart?

158
00:10:52,255 --> 00:10:53,685
I just changed my mind.

159
00:10:54,185 --> 00:10:55,185
What?

160
00:10:56,255 --> 00:10:57,525
Do you want me to say it again?

161
00:11:01,865 --> 00:11:03,065
I am not divorcing...

162
00:11:04,895 --> 00:11:05,935
you.

163
00:11:06,935 --> 00:11:09,575
That must have been a real shock for her.

164
00:11:10,205 --> 00:11:11,605
He suddenly won't get a divorce?

165
00:11:12,235 --> 00:11:15,045
The same guy who was coming out of a motel just days ago...

166
00:11:15,175 --> 00:11:17,015
with another woman?

167
00:11:17,345 --> 00:11:19,785
She must be wondering what this is all about.

168
00:11:20,045 --> 00:11:21,045
Just wait.

169
00:11:21,345 --> 00:11:23,115
Now they're the ones who will be on edge.

170
00:11:24,615 --> 00:11:25,615
Yes.

171
00:11:26,085 --> 00:11:28,655
But can we please stop talking about the motel now?

172
00:11:29,195 --> 00:11:31,795
You can never be too careful when playing with fire.

173
00:11:31,995 --> 00:11:34,495
I'm not the one playing with fire. She is.

174
00:11:36,035 --> 00:11:38,235
I never thought my wife would do something like that.

175
00:11:39,365 --> 00:11:40,665
I was so naive.

176
00:11:45,875 --> 00:11:47,675
Are you sure you can go through with this?

177
00:11:48,205 --> 00:11:51,875
- What? - Your eyes are full of regret.

178
00:11:53,185 --> 00:11:54,815
You're not ready...

179
00:11:55,815 --> 00:11:56,955
to separate.

180
00:11:59,015 --> 00:12:00,055
Are you saying that I still...

181
00:12:01,155 --> 00:12:04,055
look like I haven't been able to sort out my feelings?

182
00:12:04,395 --> 00:12:05,495
Exactly.

183
00:12:09,665 --> 00:12:12,395
Anyway, I don't want to be betrayed by my wife anymore.

184
00:12:12,935 --> 00:12:15,405
I am going to win this lawsuit. No matter what.

185
00:12:15,465 --> 00:12:18,135
Right. That's why we're using this strategy.

186
00:12:18,805 --> 00:12:19,805
But...

187
00:12:20,405 --> 00:12:22,475
you can never let them find out about this strategy.

188
00:12:24,075 --> 00:12:25,945
The fact that you said you don't want a divorce...

189
00:12:26,045 --> 00:12:29,415
was just a tactic and wasn't sincere.

190
00:12:29,585 --> 00:12:31,515
It's something they can never find out.

191
00:12:32,285 --> 00:12:34,025
Then what should I do?

192
00:12:35,525 --> 00:12:36,525
You have to move in.

193
00:12:37,895 --> 00:12:39,095
Move in where?

194
00:12:39,425 --> 00:12:42,565
To the place you'll find most uncomfortable...

195
00:12:43,535 --> 00:12:44,565
and difficult to endure.

196
00:12:45,395 --> 00:12:46,435
This lawsuit...

197
00:12:47,065 --> 00:12:48,605
is one we have to win.

198
00:12:50,205 --> 00:12:52,205
(CEO Baek Mi Young)

199
00:12:56,145 --> 00:12:59,615
So concise and straight to the point.

200
00:13:01,915 --> 00:13:03,485
In professional terms,

201
00:13:04,055 --> 00:13:05,615
we call this a betrayal.

202
00:13:07,425 --> 00:13:08,425
This won't do.

203
00:13:09,395 --> 00:13:12,225
I'll have to prepare an even more perfect brief.

204
00:13:12,595 --> 00:13:15,425
But why would he suddenly say he doesn't want a divorce?

205
00:13:16,265 --> 00:13:18,595
You don't think he actually changed his mind, do you?

206
00:13:20,465 --> 00:13:22,435
Why? Why all of a sudden?

207
00:13:22,775 --> 00:13:24,035
This is all...

208
00:13:24,335 --> 00:13:27,075
a ploy by that 200-year-old imoogi.

209
00:13:33,515 --> 00:13:34,645
It's a strategy.

210
00:13:35,485 --> 00:13:37,255
A strategy to mess with your mind.

211
00:13:37,755 --> 00:13:39,255
Mess with my mind?

212
00:13:41,925 --> 00:13:43,655
If one side holds out,

213
00:13:44,095 --> 00:13:46,895
the one with less patience is bound to give in.

214
00:13:47,225 --> 00:13:48,625
He wants you to give up on everything...

215
00:13:48,695 --> 00:13:50,935
and just beg for the divorce.

216
00:13:52,065 --> 00:13:55,105
Then he'll probably lowball you on the division of assets.

217
00:13:56,175 --> 00:13:57,835
Not to mention your management rights.

218
00:14:00,505 --> 00:14:02,945
It's not that great of a strategy.

219
00:14:02,945 --> 00:14:05,345
He's just going to wait it out...

220
00:14:05,575 --> 00:14:08,115
until you get exhausted and give in.

221
00:14:08,415 --> 00:14:09,615
So that's his game.

222
00:14:10,855 --> 00:14:11,855
It's all right.

223
00:14:12,185 --> 00:14:14,825
We'll just hit him back even harder.

224
00:14:15,995 --> 00:14:17,095
But from now on,

225
00:14:17,695 --> 00:14:20,125
you can't let your guard down, not even for a second.

226
00:14:23,595 --> 00:14:24,595
But what if...

227
00:14:25,435 --> 00:14:26,935
he means it?

228
00:14:27,835 --> 00:14:28,835
I mean,

229
00:14:30,135 --> 00:14:31,905
it might not be a strategy.

230
00:14:31,905 --> 00:14:33,645
He could actually mean it, you know.

231
00:14:34,245 --> 00:14:35,505
So you're saying...

232
00:14:36,275 --> 00:14:39,945
that there's a chance Ji Won Ho doesn't actually want a divorce?

233
00:14:40,185 --> 00:14:42,245
Of course. It's a possibility, isn't it?

234
00:14:43,515 --> 00:14:44,715
Honestly,

235
00:14:44,885 --> 00:14:46,885
you're the one who filed the lawsuit first.

236
00:14:47,255 --> 00:14:50,725
Won Ho is just in a position where he's being dragged along.

237
00:14:50,895 --> 00:14:52,355
Dragged along? Him?

238
00:14:52,425 --> 00:14:54,095
The man always does whatever he wants.

239
00:14:54,295 --> 00:14:57,595
With his personality, if Won Ho really wanted a divorce,

240
00:14:57,665 --> 00:14:59,465
he would've gone through with it by now.

241
00:15:00,665 --> 00:15:02,465
If you think about it,

242
00:15:03,035 --> 00:15:05,375
Won Ho was the one who kept putting off...

243
00:15:05,435 --> 00:15:07,075
any talk of divorce,

244
00:15:07,145 --> 00:15:08,345
using work as an excuse.

245
00:15:08,375 --> 00:15:09,945
Would someone who doesn't want a divorce...

246
00:15:10,045 --> 00:15:11,045
move out of the house...

247
00:15:11,115 --> 00:15:12,445
and live in a motel before it's even finalised?

248
00:15:12,515 --> 00:15:13,515
And if that wasn't bad enough,

249
00:15:13,515 --> 00:15:14,845
he even brought a woman to his motel.

250
00:15:14,945 --> 00:15:16,685
He brought a woman there?

251
00:15:17,815 --> 00:15:19,325
Who? When?

252
00:15:19,485 --> 00:15:20,555
There was someone.

253
00:15:20,685 --> 00:15:22,455
Are you sure it was a motel? And a woman?

254
00:15:22,655 --> 00:15:24,955
Yes. I'm telling you I saw it.

255
00:15:32,865 --> 00:15:34,035
Gosh, that's crazy.

256
00:15:34,435 --> 00:15:36,105
Did you really send that as your legal response?

257
00:15:37,035 --> 00:15:38,475
You really came out swinging.

258
00:15:38,735 --> 00:15:40,345
Yes, I talked to my lawyer,

259
00:15:40,405 --> 00:15:41,845
and he said it was the best way to go.

260
00:15:46,515 --> 00:15:49,045
Mi Young must be totally freaking out right now.

261
00:15:49,815 --> 00:15:51,085
That legal response was the first time...

262
00:15:51,155 --> 00:15:52,515
you said you didn't want a divorce, right?

263
00:15:54,125 --> 00:15:55,355
Completely out of the blue.

264
00:15:55,425 --> 00:15:56,625
Hey, if we're going to talk about that,

265
00:15:56,625 --> 00:15:59,565
think of all the bombshells Baek Mi Young has dropped on me.

266
00:15:59,995 --> 00:16:02,765
She needs to be blindsided too to know how I feel.

267
00:16:03,595 --> 00:16:06,505
But what's the plan for you and Mi Young going forward?

268
00:16:07,065 --> 00:16:08,365
What do you mean, "what's the plan?"

269
00:16:08,765 --> 00:16:09,835
With this kind of tension,

270
00:16:10,275 --> 00:16:12,035
how can you two possibly work together?

271
00:16:12,575 --> 00:16:15,445
That's her decision to make. I'm certainly not leaving.

272
00:16:18,175 --> 00:16:19,215
And...

273
00:16:19,885 --> 00:16:21,185
I'm moving back in.

274
00:16:21,685 --> 00:16:22,685
Moving back in?

275
00:16:23,185 --> 00:16:24,215
Where?

276
00:16:24,285 --> 00:16:26,285
The codename for this mission is...

277
00:16:27,355 --> 00:16:28,825
Sleeping with the Enemy.

278
00:16:39,435 --> 00:16:40,905
He wants you to give up on everything...

279
00:16:40,965 --> 00:16:43,175
and just beg for the divorce.

280
00:16:43,575 --> 00:16:46,545
Then he'll probably lowball you on the division of assets.

281
00:16:47,305 --> 00:16:48,845
Not to mention your management rights.

282
00:16:50,015 --> 00:16:52,175
He wouldn't go that far, would he?

283
00:16:53,115 --> 00:16:54,345
Do you want me to say it again?

284
00:16:54,615 --> 00:16:55,845
I am not divorcing...

285
00:16:56,785 --> 00:16:57,785
you.

286
00:16:58,955 --> 00:17:00,155
That crazy...

287
00:17:03,825 --> 00:17:04,825
Ji Won Ho.

288
00:17:05,095 --> 00:17:07,325
So you're going to play dirty, is that it?

289
00:17:14,135 --> 00:17:15,135
(Please try again.)

290
00:17:16,035 --> 00:17:17,035
Why isn't this working?

291
00:17:27,745 --> 00:17:28,745
What the...

292
00:17:29,345 --> 00:17:30,585
Did you change the password?

293
00:17:31,455 --> 00:17:32,455
What are you doing here?

294
00:17:32,515 --> 00:17:34,425
Why did you change the password?

295
00:17:41,925 --> 00:17:43,735
What's this about? Why are you here?

296
00:17:43,865 --> 00:17:46,135
Why am I here? This is my house. Do I need to ask for permission?

297
00:17:47,205 --> 00:17:49,065
What are you waiting for? Open the door.

298
00:17:51,205 --> 00:17:52,975
Open it. Now.

299
00:18:02,445 --> 00:18:04,315
Good grief. Hey, what is wrong with you?

300
00:18:04,685 --> 00:18:06,655
Wait, did you really just let yourself in?

301
00:18:08,185 --> 00:18:09,255
Hey!

302
00:18:09,325 --> 00:18:10,995
Are you really not going to divorce me?

303
00:18:11,625 --> 00:18:12,925
Hey, Ji Won Ho!

304
00:18:15,825 --> 00:18:16,835
What the...

305
00:18:20,465 --> 00:18:22,435
He's lost his mind.

306
00:18:23,135 --> 00:18:25,675
CEO Ji showed up at your house in the middle of the night?

307
00:18:26,145 --> 00:18:27,245
Yes.

308
00:18:28,145 --> 00:18:29,275
What did he say?

309
00:18:29,845 --> 00:18:32,115
That he wants to get back together?

310
00:18:33,345 --> 00:18:34,415
Then why?

311
00:18:34,845 --> 00:18:36,255
Why did he suddenly barge in like that?

312
00:18:36,615 --> 00:18:38,615
He said he came because it's his house.

313
00:18:39,055 --> 00:18:40,055
Right.

314
00:18:40,625 --> 00:18:42,255
He's not wrong about that.

315
00:18:43,095 --> 00:18:44,655
But...

316
00:18:45,025 --> 00:18:46,795
if you're really getting a divorce,

317
00:18:47,365 --> 00:18:49,595
isn't that an incredibly uncomfortable situation?

318
00:18:49,695 --> 00:18:50,995
Tell me about it.

319
00:18:51,135 --> 00:18:53,405
If this goes on, we'll be stuck together 24 hours a day.

320
00:18:53,635 --> 00:18:56,135
How did I live with Ji Won Ho for seven years?

321
00:18:58,575 --> 00:19:00,775
This really is Sleeping with the Enemy.

322
00:19:02,175 --> 00:19:03,945
It must have been so awkward yesterday.

323
00:19:05,075 --> 00:19:06,285
I bet you didn't get a wink of sleep.

324
00:19:07,215 --> 00:19:08,415
Why wouldn't I have?

325
00:19:08,485 --> 00:19:09,855
We've always slept in separate rooms.

326
00:19:10,215 --> 00:19:11,255
Right.

327
00:19:11,655 --> 00:19:14,185
I guess you two were always used to being uncomfortable.

328
00:19:14,985 --> 00:19:16,355
Why are you bringing that up now?

329
00:19:16,755 --> 00:19:18,025
Anyway, be careful.

330
00:19:18,325 --> 00:19:19,895
If you're not careful in this situation,

331
00:19:19,965 --> 00:19:21,495
you could take a big hit too.

332
00:19:21,725 --> 00:19:22,795
I know.

333
00:19:24,265 --> 00:19:26,065
I'll be careful handling the fire.

334
00:19:32,175 --> 00:19:34,775
CEO Ji, I have something to tell you.

335
00:19:35,275 --> 00:19:37,115
Can we meet for a moment today?

336
00:19:37,945 --> 00:19:39,015
Oh, boy.

337
00:19:40,085 --> 00:19:42,015
Now how do I put out this fire?

338
00:19:43,055 --> 00:19:44,055
Fire?

339
00:19:44,285 --> 00:19:46,555
Yes, a matchstick from Milan.

340
00:19:48,185 --> 00:19:49,595
I'm an orphan now.

341
00:19:51,195 --> 00:19:53,495
An orphan? What do you mean by that?

342
00:19:53,865 --> 00:19:54,895
My dad...

343
00:19:55,565 --> 00:19:57,065
told me to never contact him again.

344
00:19:58,035 --> 00:19:59,865
And to not even look for him as long as he lives.

345
00:20:00,465 --> 00:20:01,935
Your father? But why?

346
00:20:03,805 --> 00:20:05,175
A little while ago,

347
00:20:05,605 --> 00:20:07,975
I contacted him because it was the anniversary of my mom's death.

348
00:20:08,875 --> 00:20:10,715
Apparently, they had a huge fight because of it.

349
00:20:12,575 --> 00:20:15,045
He said he doesn't want any more trouble because of me.

350
00:20:28,525 --> 00:20:29,565
Are you okay?

351
00:20:30,835 --> 00:20:32,165
Of course I'm not okay.

352
00:20:35,265 --> 00:20:36,475
That's awful.

353
00:20:40,345 --> 00:20:41,345
Could you...

354
00:20:42,505 --> 00:20:44,045
be my friend?

355
00:20:45,245 --> 00:20:46,245
A friend?

356
00:20:46,585 --> 00:20:48,585
I don't have anyone around...

357
00:20:48,945 --> 00:20:51,155
who I can have a deep conversation with like this.

358
00:20:51,685 --> 00:20:54,325
I just want to meet with you every now and then...

359
00:20:54,485 --> 00:20:56,425
and open up about what's on my mind.

360
00:20:57,825 --> 00:20:59,295
I feel like I could finally live then.

361
00:21:06,505 --> 00:21:07,865
Then promise me one thing.

362
00:21:10,175 --> 00:21:11,835
From now on, no more saying you like me...

363
00:21:11,905 --> 00:21:13,375
or any other strange things.

364
00:21:13,605 --> 00:21:15,775
And that we will never be more than friends.

365
00:21:19,445 --> 00:21:20,445
Okay.

366
00:21:21,245 --> 00:21:24,215
You haven't eaten yet, have you? Let's go get something to eat.

367
00:21:33,925 --> 00:21:36,165
This is so good. Totally my style.

368
00:21:38,095 --> 00:21:39,095
Really?

369
00:21:39,805 --> 00:21:40,905
What about it is your style?

370
00:21:47,975 --> 00:21:48,975
Hey.

371
00:21:50,645 --> 00:21:53,315
It's spicy. You eat it. What is this?

372
00:22:03,495 --> 00:22:05,395
Gosh, it's so sweet.

373
00:22:07,565 --> 00:22:08,565
You eat all of this.

374
00:22:08,725 --> 00:22:09,835
What are you laughing at?

375
00:22:12,235 --> 00:22:14,735
- Win! - Win!

376
00:22:14,935 --> 00:22:16,135
- Win! - Win!

377
00:22:22,045 --> 00:22:23,345
CEO Ji, you do it too.

378
00:22:25,015 --> 00:22:27,385
Why do you even want to do this?

379
00:22:27,445 --> 00:22:28,645
Look into my eyes for three seconds.

380
00:22:28,785 --> 00:22:30,085
One, two, three. Happy now?

381
00:22:30,785 --> 00:22:33,355
Let's stop now. I'm seriously exhausted.

382
00:22:33,425 --> 00:22:34,555
Your hat came off.

383
00:22:37,355 --> 00:22:38,795
Let's go for one more round.

384
00:22:42,095 --> 00:22:43,695
- I'm all set. - Why?

385
00:22:43,765 --> 00:22:45,495
- The lens over there. - One, two, three.

386
00:22:45,565 --> 00:22:47,135
One, two, three...

387
00:22:47,435 --> 00:22:49,335
- Bend down. - Oh, my back.

388
00:22:50,275 --> 00:22:52,135
- One, two, three. - Okay.

389
00:22:52,835 --> 00:22:53,845
Two, three.

390
00:23:06,215 --> 00:23:07,225
Unbelievable.

391
00:23:08,985 --> 00:23:09,995
Darn it.

392
00:23:12,095 --> 00:23:13,695
Hey, let's clock out together.

393
00:23:13,695 --> 00:23:15,165
Hey, I'm leaving first. See you tomorrow.

394
00:23:27,775 --> 00:23:29,845
Why did you call me out today?

395
00:23:30,275 --> 00:23:31,275
Why?

396
00:23:31,975 --> 00:23:33,245
There's no particular reason.

397
00:23:33,785 --> 00:23:34,785
What?

398
00:23:34,985 --> 00:23:36,615
We're friends, aren't we?

399
00:23:37,355 --> 00:23:39,115
Friends can just meet up...

400
00:23:39,285 --> 00:23:41,585
and have a drink for no reason.

401
00:23:43,655 --> 00:23:45,655
How could I ever win an argument with you?

402
00:23:47,425 --> 00:23:48,625
Then for today,

403
00:23:49,525 --> 00:23:51,095
why don't you try to beat me at drinking?

404
00:23:52,765 --> 00:23:53,765
What do you say?

405
00:23:54,205 --> 00:23:55,335
The loser...

406
00:23:56,575 --> 00:23:57,635
pays for the drinks.

407
00:23:58,275 --> 00:23:59,275
Unbelievable.

408
00:24:02,875 --> 00:24:03,875
You're on.

409
00:24:05,345 --> 00:24:06,345
Come on.

410
00:24:06,415 --> 00:24:07,545
I didn't pay for the drinks.

411
00:24:07,985 --> 00:24:08,985
No.

412
00:24:11,515 --> 00:24:12,685
I have to go back...

413
00:24:13,825 --> 00:24:15,285
Let's go for round two.

414
00:24:15,285 --> 00:24:17,125
CEO Ji, you'll die if you drink more.

415
00:24:17,195 --> 00:24:19,895
What? Who's going to die? I'm perfectly fine.

416
00:24:19,965 --> 00:24:22,265
CEO Ji, is this the right place?

417
00:24:22,325 --> 00:24:24,435
Yes, that's right. This is it.

418
00:24:24,995 --> 00:24:26,495
Yes, just a moment.

419
00:24:27,735 --> 00:24:29,535
This thing, hold on, this...

420
00:24:34,775 --> 00:24:35,805
Hang on.

421
00:24:37,115 --> 00:24:38,515
This is...

422
00:24:39,515 --> 00:24:42,115
- Goodness. - Gosh.

423
00:24:48,025 --> 00:24:51,425
- CEO Ji. - Let's have a drink at my place.

424
00:24:51,555 --> 00:24:55,065
Have a drink. Everybody, have a drink...

425
00:24:55,825 --> 00:24:57,995
Have a drink. My back hurts.

426
00:24:58,395 --> 00:25:01,505
Oh, my back. It hurts. Oh, darn it...

427
00:25:01,765 --> 00:25:04,335
- It hurts. Oh, man, it hurts. - Hey.

428
00:25:04,405 --> 00:25:06,745
Ji Won Ho. Are you out of your mind?

429
00:25:06,805 --> 00:25:08,345
Get me some water...

430
00:25:08,605 --> 00:25:09,875
Get me some water.

431
00:25:09,945 --> 00:25:10,945
Get me some water...

432
00:25:16,215 --> 00:25:18,285
Of all the ridiculous things...

433
00:25:18,585 --> 00:25:20,755
I mean, the motel was one thing,

434
00:25:20,885 --> 00:25:23,425
but to actually bring a woman into our house.

435
00:25:23,595 --> 00:25:26,255
- I mean, isn't that crazy? - He's insane.

436
00:25:26,895 --> 00:25:29,265
It's like a scene from some trashy soap opera.

437
00:25:29,395 --> 00:25:31,995
The way that woman looked at me...

438
00:25:33,605 --> 00:25:35,965
My blood boils just thinking about it.

439
00:25:37,875 --> 00:25:39,505
I'm not overreacting, am I?

440
00:25:39,605 --> 00:25:41,675
Not at all. You are definitely not overreacting.

441
00:25:42,345 --> 00:25:45,375
All right. Let's use this energy...

442
00:25:45,445 --> 00:25:47,215
and try to write your statement.

443
00:25:50,715 --> 00:25:54,255
From the beginning, recall the anger you felt then.

444
00:25:54,255 --> 00:25:56,725
It helps if you can make it sound a bit more provocative.

445
00:25:56,825 --> 00:25:58,125
Well,

446
00:25:58,355 --> 00:26:01,165
it was like the two of them were a single entity,

447
00:26:01,225 --> 00:26:03,565
tumbling through the front gate in a heap.

448
00:26:04,365 --> 00:26:07,765
And then that tramp looked at me in this odd way,

449
00:26:07,835 --> 00:26:09,265
while holding onto Ji Won Ho's pants,

450
00:26:09,335 --> 00:26:10,335
as he was yelling for water.

451
00:26:10,905 --> 00:26:12,275
Wait, this isn't the problem.

452
00:26:12,275 --> 00:26:13,745
You've met my mother-in-law, right?

453
00:26:14,205 --> 00:26:16,275
That time we went to his parents' house.

454
00:26:17,175 --> 00:26:18,275
Mi Young,

455
00:26:18,345 --> 00:26:20,315
you're going to make me a birthday meal yourself?

456
00:26:20,385 --> 00:26:22,285
I can help with that...

457
00:26:23,455 --> 00:26:26,085
Your back is acting up, what are you trying to do?

458
00:26:26,185 --> 00:26:27,825
You need to rest. Don't help.

459
00:26:27,955 --> 00:26:29,725
Have you given up on having a child?

460
00:26:30,295 --> 00:26:31,755
- Pardon? - Don't tell me you've given up...

461
00:26:31,755 --> 00:26:33,195
just because you failed once, have you?

462
00:26:34,625 --> 00:26:37,195
A child who looks like Won Ho would be so smart and beautiful.

463
00:26:37,695 --> 00:26:40,005
The plaintiff suffered interference, neglect, and insults...

464
00:26:40,005 --> 00:26:41,465
from her mother-in-law.

465
00:26:41,705 --> 00:26:43,735
She was treated in a severely unfair manner.

466
00:26:44,205 --> 00:26:47,605
- What is it now? - I feel sorry for you.

467
00:26:48,075 --> 00:26:49,645
You never even met your in-laws.

468
00:26:50,115 --> 00:26:52,545
I mean, how could they die so tragically like that?

469
00:26:52,775 --> 00:26:54,585
The mother-in-law, who disliked the plaintiff...

470
00:26:54,585 --> 00:26:55,685
even before the marriage...

471
00:26:55,985 --> 00:26:57,385
Mi Young, did you say that to Won Ho,

472
00:26:57,615 --> 00:26:59,755
that you're not getting pregnant because I'm stressing you out?

473
00:27:00,085 --> 00:27:01,725
- Excuse me? - Throughout the marriage,

474
00:27:01,725 --> 00:27:03,155
she habitually disrespected...

475
00:27:03,225 --> 00:27:05,125
and verbally abused the plaintiff and her family.

476
00:27:05,325 --> 00:27:06,865
Because you're always so focused on your image,

477
00:27:06,865 --> 00:27:09,165
my mom thinks she can walk all over you.

478
00:27:09,425 --> 00:27:11,335
I told you not to go there.

479
00:27:11,465 --> 00:27:13,505
You have no problem arguing back with me.

480
00:27:13,665 --> 00:27:17,275
In response to this, the defendant consistently turned a blind eye...

481
00:27:17,535 --> 00:27:19,275
and remained a passive bystander.

482
00:27:19,335 --> 00:27:21,375
I'm absolutely not changing it.

483
00:27:21,575 --> 00:27:23,675
Not without a request from Man Ju. Not even if the sky falls.

484
00:27:23,745 --> 00:27:26,815
Furthermore, the plaintiff was never once...

485
00:27:26,945 --> 00:27:29,685
treated as anything more than a business partner by the defendant,

486
00:27:30,485 --> 00:27:32,855
and despite the plaintiff's frequent hospitalizations...

487
00:27:32,855 --> 00:27:34,055
due to her poor health,

488
00:27:34,155 --> 00:27:35,885
she has no memory of ever receiving care...

489
00:27:35,885 --> 00:27:37,695
or consideration from the defendant.

490
00:27:37,895 --> 00:27:39,855
Throughout the marriage, the defendant...

491
00:27:39,955 --> 00:27:41,695
was indifferent to the plaintiff.

492
00:27:42,925 --> 00:27:45,435
The defendant's mood swings were so severe...

493
00:27:45,435 --> 00:27:47,235
as to suggest intermittent explosive disorder,

494
00:27:47,605 --> 00:27:49,765
and whenever he was unable to control his emotions,

495
00:27:49,765 --> 00:27:51,135
he would direct his anger at the plaintiff...

496
00:27:51,135 --> 00:27:53,605
through direct and indirect acts of violence.

497
00:27:54,975 --> 00:27:57,775
Eventually, this led the plaintiff to seek psychiatric help,

498
00:27:58,675 --> 00:28:00,815
and she was diagnosed with a panic disorder.

499
00:28:04,215 --> 00:28:05,955
The decisive moment that ruined the plaintiff's relationship...

500
00:28:05,955 --> 00:28:07,355
with the defendant,

501
00:28:07,825 --> 00:28:09,625
was an incident of physical assault.

502
00:28:11,725 --> 00:28:14,395
At that time, the defendant caused harm to the plaintiff's body...

503
00:28:14,395 --> 00:28:15,995
that were severe enough to cause deep bruising.

504
00:28:17,135 --> 00:28:18,665
The plaintiff and defendant...

505
00:28:19,295 --> 00:28:21,905
began sleeping in separate rooms after this incident.

506
00:28:23,435 --> 00:28:25,435
The plaintiff tried to resolve the issue...

507
00:28:25,435 --> 00:28:27,205
amicably through conversation,

508
00:28:27,745 --> 00:28:29,405
but the defendant refused to do so.

509
00:28:30,145 --> 00:28:33,315
Even though their marriage had effectively ended,

510
00:28:33,585 --> 00:28:35,585
the plaintiff continued to try out of her love for their business...

511
00:28:35,645 --> 00:28:39,155
and her desire to keep their family together.

512
00:28:40,525 --> 00:28:41,825
Oh, crap. One more time.

513
00:28:42,925 --> 00:28:44,025
Come on.

514
00:28:47,895 --> 00:28:50,365
No way. That's amazing. Really?

515
00:28:51,535 --> 00:28:53,935
You went all the way out there just to take photos for work?

516
00:28:54,765 --> 00:28:57,005
I know. The scenery there is killer.

517
00:28:58,275 --> 00:28:59,705
That must have been so fun.

518
00:28:59,835 --> 00:29:01,575
All right. See you at the office tomorrow.

519
00:29:01,805 --> 00:29:02,805
Later.

520
00:29:03,875 --> 00:29:04,875
Hey!

521
00:29:05,875 --> 00:29:06,915
Keep it down.

522
00:29:07,485 --> 00:29:09,815
I can't sleep because of your game.

523
00:29:10,015 --> 00:29:12,485
What are you talking about? Your voice is way louder right now.

524
00:29:12,555 --> 00:29:14,755
The neighbours will complain again.

525
00:29:14,755 --> 00:29:15,785
What?

526
00:29:16,055 --> 00:29:17,755
Come out. Now.

527
00:29:17,995 --> 00:29:19,055
Let's talk outside.

528
00:29:20,625 --> 00:29:22,425
Fine. Let's have a nice chat outside.

529
00:29:22,495 --> 00:29:24,265
What, you think I'm scared?

530
00:29:30,935 --> 00:29:33,545
Hey, is this why you moved back in?

531
00:29:33,605 --> 00:29:36,205
What? What am I supposed to have done now?

532
00:29:36,275 --> 00:29:39,445
Giggling with that young girl. You're doing it on purpose.

533
00:29:39,445 --> 00:29:40,585
What are you talking about?

534
00:29:40,585 --> 00:29:42,885
Who's the one always stuck to Calvin's side?

535
00:29:42,945 --> 00:29:45,085
What, "stuck to his side"? Have you said your piece?

536
00:29:45,155 --> 00:29:47,525
Yes, stuck to his side. Clinging to him just like this.

537
00:29:47,585 --> 00:29:49,155
Unbelievable. You're one to talk...

538
00:29:49,155 --> 00:29:51,525
after bringing a woman to our front door.

539
00:29:51,625 --> 00:29:53,665
If you're jealous, go ahead and bring someone over.

540
00:29:53,865 --> 00:29:56,295
What? Hey, you think I couldn't if I wanted to?

541
00:29:56,365 --> 00:29:58,035
Go ahead and bring Calvin over.

542
00:29:58,035 --> 00:30:00,135
If I brought men over, I'd have brought a truckload by now.

543
00:30:00,205 --> 00:30:01,735
Then bring them right to the front door.

544
00:30:01,805 --> 00:30:03,575
I swear, I can't believe you.

545
00:30:03,635 --> 00:30:05,775
- Violence? - Hey. You're having an affair.

546
00:30:05,835 --> 00:30:08,205
- Add it. Go on, add it. - You want me to actually hit you?

547
00:30:08,275 --> 00:30:09,475
People will report you for this.

548
00:30:11,275 --> 00:30:12,275
Go on, hit me.

549
00:30:12,345 --> 00:30:14,185
- Come on. - You're so annoying. Get away.

550
00:30:14,245 --> 00:30:15,245
Hit me.

551
00:30:15,715 --> 00:30:16,845
Oh my, really?

552
00:30:17,415 --> 00:30:19,385
You both came down with bad body aches?

553
00:30:19,955 --> 00:30:22,985
Right, no wonder. The wind was chilly yesterday.

554
00:30:23,995 --> 00:30:25,825
Are you sure you don't need to see a doctor?

555
00:30:26,525 --> 00:30:27,525
Both of them?

556
00:30:30,165 --> 00:30:31,595
Okay, I understand.

557
00:30:31,965 --> 00:30:34,635
Don't worry about the store, and get some rest.

558
00:30:37,605 --> 00:30:38,605
Body aches?

559
00:30:38,675 --> 00:30:40,305
Both CEO Ji and CEO Baek...

560
00:30:40,375 --> 00:30:42,775
seem to have come down with a bad cold and body aches.

561
00:30:43,005 --> 00:30:45,675
They got sick as soon as they started living together.

562
00:30:45,845 --> 00:30:47,185
Oh my goodness.

563
00:30:47,245 --> 00:30:50,455
You don't think CEO Ji put something in Mi Young's food, do you?

564
00:30:51,285 --> 00:30:54,055
How can you say something like that so casually?

565
00:30:55,285 --> 00:30:57,725
It was a joke. A joke.

566
00:30:58,025 --> 00:30:59,395
Even if it's a joke,

567
00:30:59,455 --> 00:31:00,925
there are some things you just shouldn't say.

568
00:31:02,925 --> 00:31:04,265
All right.

569
00:31:04,635 --> 00:31:06,165
I'll be more careful.

570
00:31:08,335 --> 00:31:09,465
Calvin.

571
00:31:13,805 --> 00:31:15,775
- Hello. - Hi.

572
00:31:15,845 --> 00:31:17,175
But what should we do?

573
00:31:17,245 --> 00:31:20,385
CEO Baek was sick today, so she couldn't come in.

574
00:31:20,645 --> 00:31:23,085
Mi Young is sick?

575
00:32:10,935 --> 00:32:12,195
Hee Ju.

576
00:32:14,935 --> 00:32:17,335
No, it's fine. A get-well visit? Don't be silly.

577
00:32:23,605 --> 00:32:25,075
Calvin.

578
00:32:26,145 --> 00:32:28,945
I am a little sick,

579
00:32:30,215 --> 00:32:32,315
but there's no need to worry so much.

580
00:32:34,155 --> 00:32:35,155
Really?

581
00:32:35,685 --> 00:32:37,955
Well, you can stop by for a little while then.

582
00:32:42,325 --> 00:32:45,565
Okay. I'd appreciate it if you came.

583
00:32:45,695 --> 00:32:46,895
See you later then.

584
00:32:48,635 --> 00:32:50,335
Okay. Be careful on your way.

585
00:32:50,835 --> 00:32:51,835
Okay.

586
00:33:00,415 --> 00:33:03,115
(Maesan Apartments)

587
00:33:03,185 --> 00:33:05,655
(A Day for Porridge)

588
00:33:10,695 --> 00:33:11,995
Oh, you bought flowers?

589
00:33:15,665 --> 00:33:16,995
Oh, porridge?

590
00:33:43,855 --> 00:33:45,055
That looks delicious.

591
00:33:46,855 --> 00:33:48,965
It's okay. I'll eat it.

592
00:33:53,905 --> 00:33:55,865
I'll give him this, the guy has some class.

593
00:33:58,905 --> 00:34:00,135
Oh, thanks.

594
00:34:04,375 --> 00:34:05,515
Is there anything you want to eat?

595
00:34:06,975 --> 00:34:09,145
Oh, I'm fine.

596
00:34:09,215 --> 00:34:11,155
No, you're not. You need to eat to get your strength back.

597
00:34:11,415 --> 00:34:12,415
Hold on.

598
00:34:12,485 --> 00:34:13,585
I'll order something.

599
00:34:14,185 --> 00:34:15,325
Are you...

600
00:34:15,555 --> 00:34:16,985
in the mood for some dessert?

601
00:34:17,525 --> 00:34:19,155
No, I'm okay...

602
00:34:19,325 --> 00:34:21,925
A little sugar will help you get your energy back.

603
00:34:50,955 --> 00:34:53,495
How long have you known CEO Ji?

604
00:34:54,165 --> 00:34:57,095
We've known each other for a while. About eight years?

605
00:34:57,365 --> 00:34:58,465
Oh, really?

606
00:34:58,835 --> 00:34:59,995
What about you?

607
00:35:00,395 --> 00:35:02,435
Longer than you have.

608
00:35:02,935 --> 00:35:04,135
By any chance,

609
00:35:04,135 --> 00:35:06,005
are you CEO Baek's ex-boyfriend?

610
00:35:10,005 --> 00:35:11,345
I see.

611
00:35:11,915 --> 00:35:13,775
That's why she was acting awkward.

612
00:35:14,045 --> 00:35:16,445
Awkward? Do we seem awkward?

613
00:35:16,615 --> 00:35:17,815
CEO Baek and I.

614
00:35:18,415 --> 00:35:20,155
It's the fact that your feelings for CEO Baek...

615
00:35:20,215 --> 00:35:22,855
are so one-sided. That's what's awkward.

616
00:35:23,125 --> 00:35:24,495
And you, Hee Ju?

617
00:35:24,825 --> 00:35:27,225
At this rate, you're practically CEO Ji's stalker, aren't you?

618
00:35:27,865 --> 00:35:29,095
A stalker?

619
00:35:31,435 --> 00:35:32,495
Look who's talking.

620
00:35:33,035 --> 00:35:34,035
Excuse me?

621
00:35:34,565 --> 00:35:35,865
I know everything.

622
00:35:36,265 --> 00:35:38,675
I heard you asked Man Ju...

623
00:35:38,735 --> 00:35:41,045
to send an invitation to CEO Baek.

624
00:35:42,075 --> 00:35:44,145
At least I'm a straightforward person.

625
00:35:44,875 --> 00:35:46,575
Unlike you, I'm not devious.

626
00:35:46,645 --> 00:35:48,515
I don't manipulate people behind their backs.

627
00:35:50,815 --> 00:35:51,985
Manipulate?

628
00:35:52,355 --> 00:35:54,255
I am actually holding myself back.

629
00:35:55,155 --> 00:35:57,425
All I want is for Mi Young to be happy.

630
00:35:57,625 --> 00:35:59,255
That's the only thing that matters.

631
00:36:02,065 --> 00:36:03,125
Well,

632
00:36:03,825 --> 00:36:06,035
I believe you have to fight for love, but...

633
00:36:06,835 --> 00:36:08,935
I'll respect your values.

634
00:36:26,785 --> 00:36:30,085
I have to say, CEO Ji seems like the better man.

635
00:36:30,695 --> 00:36:34,295
- Excuse me? - CEO Ji is much better than Calvin.

636
00:36:34,425 --> 00:36:36,365
Whether as a partner or anything else.

637
00:36:37,435 --> 00:36:38,995
Is that why you...

638
00:36:39,065 --> 00:36:40,905
transferred to CEO Ji?

639
00:36:41,135 --> 00:36:42,205
Transferred?

640
00:36:42,205 --> 00:36:44,535
You'll probably transfer post-divorce anyway.

641
00:36:46,305 --> 00:36:49,305
Personally, I wouldn't recommend CEO Calvin.

642
00:36:50,405 --> 00:36:51,445
He has no appeal.

643
00:36:54,045 --> 00:36:56,815
Then what charms does Ji Won Ho have for you?

644
00:36:57,015 --> 00:36:58,615
He has plenty of charm.

645
00:36:59,385 --> 00:37:00,725
More than I can count.

646
00:37:01,855 --> 00:37:03,425
CEO Ji...

647
00:37:04,055 --> 00:37:05,795
has a charm that never runs out.

648
00:37:07,095 --> 00:37:09,395
The more I see him, the more I want him.

649
00:37:10,425 --> 00:37:11,435
Then take him.

650
00:37:12,695 --> 00:37:14,565
I can really have him?

651
00:37:15,035 --> 00:37:16,265
Take him if you can.

652
00:37:16,935 --> 00:37:19,205
I sent him back for a refund a long time ago.

653
00:37:28,785 --> 00:37:30,115
Is that your type?

654
00:37:31,415 --> 00:37:34,025
- Excuse me? - She's so young and brazen.

655
00:37:35,185 --> 00:37:37,025
I found her exhausting to deal with.

656
00:37:39,255 --> 00:37:42,795
And what about you, Calvin? Are your tastes still as unwavering?

657
00:37:43,765 --> 00:37:46,235
- Pardon? - Is that why you came back?

658
00:37:46,635 --> 00:37:48,105
To reclaim that unwavering taste of yours.

659
00:37:48,535 --> 00:37:50,875
Think whatever you want.

660
00:37:52,935 --> 00:37:53,935
By the way...

661
00:37:56,775 --> 00:37:58,645
Do you remember a promise I made?

662
00:37:59,675 --> 00:38:00,685
Promise?

663
00:38:01,145 --> 00:38:04,815
The promise we made at the food stall seven years ago.

664
00:38:06,855 --> 00:38:10,155
I'm thinking of keeping that promise soon.

665
00:38:22,865 --> 00:38:25,475
Ha Neul, Grandma will give you some later,

666
00:38:25,535 --> 00:38:27,105
so stop eating for now.

667
00:38:27,645 --> 00:38:28,945
I'm hungry.

668
00:38:29,245 --> 00:38:32,915
Goodness, you just ate. How can you still be hungry?

669
00:38:36,985 --> 00:38:37,985
Oh, good grief.

670
00:38:38,155 --> 00:38:41,655
He's his father's son, all right, with that appetite.

671
00:38:41,725 --> 00:38:42,725
Honestly.

672
00:38:45,155 --> 00:38:47,425
Mom, what is all this?

673
00:38:47,695 --> 00:38:50,465
This? I'm taking it to Won Ho's house.

674
00:38:50,935 --> 00:38:52,535
You're going to give all this food to Won Ho?

675
00:38:52,865 --> 00:38:54,935
Mom, there's no way Won Ho can eat all this.

676
00:38:55,135 --> 00:38:56,535
Who said it was all for Won Ho?

677
00:38:56,665 --> 00:38:57,975
Is he the only one eating in that house?

678
00:38:58,305 --> 00:38:59,605
You made this for Mi Young too?

679
00:39:00,135 --> 00:39:03,075
- What's the occasion? - This won't fit in the fridge.

680
00:39:03,245 --> 00:39:04,575
I'll have to leave some of it on the balcony.

681
00:39:04,815 --> 00:39:06,645
Are you going to deliver this to Won Ho's yourself?

682
00:39:06,975 --> 00:39:08,185
Just have it delivered.

683
00:39:08,245 --> 00:39:10,545
Come on, I'm sure Mi Young wouldn't be happy to see you.

684
00:39:10,755 --> 00:39:11,755
What did you say, you brat?

685
00:39:15,585 --> 00:39:17,925
My mom's such an amazing cook.

686
00:39:17,995 --> 00:39:19,425
Gosh. At least you know that.

687
00:39:19,925 --> 00:39:21,725
- Just one. - Hey!

688
00:39:39,015 --> 00:39:40,545
It's getting late. Aren't you going home?

689
00:39:41,245 --> 00:39:42,545
I can't be the only one to leave.

690
00:39:43,885 --> 00:39:45,585
Hee Ju, aren't you going home?

691
00:39:45,955 --> 00:39:47,455
I can handle it myself.

692
00:40:02,435 --> 00:40:03,435
Hi, Mom.

693
00:40:04,775 --> 00:40:05,775
I am. Why?

694
00:40:07,475 --> 00:40:08,705
What?

695
00:40:09,145 --> 00:40:10,975
You're bringing side dishes over to the house now?

696
00:40:12,175 --> 00:40:14,515
Okay, sure. Be careful on your way.

697
00:40:15,485 --> 00:40:16,485
Okay.

698
00:40:18,855 --> 00:40:22,055
Listen, my mother is on her way to my house.

699
00:40:22,125 --> 00:40:23,425
Well, I should get going then.

700
00:40:23,485 --> 00:40:25,355
Me too. I'll get going.

701
00:40:28,825 --> 00:40:30,365
I should probably grab a cab.

702
00:40:32,135 --> 00:40:33,635
Hey, where are you going in the middle of the night?

703
00:40:33,865 --> 00:40:35,365
I'm just going to head to A Ri's place.

704
00:40:35,565 --> 00:40:37,165
Wait, why all of a sudden?

705
00:40:37,165 --> 00:40:38,605
Didn't you hear my mom was coming over?

706
00:40:39,405 --> 00:40:42,005
That's exactly why I'm leaving. Because she's coming.

707
00:40:42,245 --> 00:40:44,375
Mom is coming because she knows you're home.

708
00:40:44,445 --> 00:40:45,975
She's bringing us side dishes.

709
00:40:46,215 --> 00:40:48,245
I'm sorry, but I never asked your mother...

710
00:40:48,245 --> 00:40:49,945
to bring me side dishes,

711
00:40:50,715 --> 00:40:52,315
and I have no desire to eat her side dishes.

712
00:40:54,155 --> 00:40:57,125
Mi Young, my mom is still your mother-in-law.

713
00:40:57,325 --> 00:40:59,725
No matter what, shouldn't you do the decent thing?

714
00:41:00,255 --> 00:41:02,795
That's why I'm avoiding her. To do the decent thing.

715
00:41:04,465 --> 00:41:05,495
What?

716
00:41:05,495 --> 00:41:07,635
If your mother grabs my hair again,

717
00:41:08,105 --> 00:41:09,635
I don't think I'll be able to stay quiet today.

718
00:41:10,335 --> 00:41:12,275
Oh? I got a cab.

719
00:41:13,135 --> 00:41:16,245
I'm staying at A Ri's tonight. I'm going to pack my things and go.

720
00:41:25,215 --> 00:41:27,555
All right, it's about time we wrote our reply.

721
00:41:29,025 --> 00:41:32,855
They sent over the grounds for divorce, item by item.

722
00:41:33,555 --> 00:41:35,295
I can let the rest of it slide,

723
00:41:36,425 --> 00:41:37,835
but this part bothers me a little.

724
00:41:39,035 --> 00:41:42,135
"The definitive moment the couple's relationship began to fall apart..."

725
00:41:42,305 --> 00:41:45,605
"was the assault incident."

726
00:41:48,605 --> 00:41:51,615
Why did you beat her until she was covered in bruises?

727
00:41:52,145 --> 00:41:53,275
Covered in bruises?

728
00:41:54,115 --> 00:41:55,115
That's what it says.

729
00:41:56,585 --> 00:41:58,385
That she was covered in bruises.

730
00:42:01,485 --> 00:42:02,485
No, that's not what happened.

731
00:42:04,025 --> 00:42:07,125
So you're saying you just stood there...

732
00:42:07,765 --> 00:42:10,265
and your wife just happened to get bruised?

733
00:42:17,775 --> 00:42:20,375
To be clear, I absolutely did not hit her.

734
00:42:21,405 --> 00:42:23,975
I was trying to stop her. That's how it happened.

735
00:42:25,575 --> 00:42:27,585
She was threatening to kill herself, waving a knife around.

736
00:42:27,645 --> 00:42:28,845
What was I supposed to do, not stop her?

737
00:42:28,945 --> 00:42:30,915
I was trying my best to get the knife away from her...

738
00:42:31,755 --> 00:42:32,755
In the process...

739
00:42:37,795 --> 00:42:38,795
She had a knife?

740
00:42:39,555 --> 00:42:41,295
(Bae Su Ji Law Office)

741
00:42:42,025 --> 00:42:43,225
The conflict between the plaintiff...

742
00:42:43,295 --> 00:42:44,795
and the defendant's mother was not severe,

743
00:42:45,095 --> 00:42:47,165
and the plaintiff was also responsible for the conflict.

744
00:42:49,665 --> 00:42:50,665
What?

745
00:42:51,375 --> 00:42:53,305
Oh, you're asking if I'm coming home for the holiday?

746
00:42:55,405 --> 00:42:57,675
The plaintiff used her busy work schedule as an excuse...

747
00:42:57,945 --> 00:43:00,145
and rarely called the defendant's parents,

748
00:43:00,745 --> 00:43:03,085
but the defendant tried to be understanding of the plaintiff...

749
00:43:03,415 --> 00:43:05,915
and never once took his mother's side.

750
00:43:06,055 --> 00:43:07,315
No. I'm sorry.

751
00:43:08,355 --> 00:43:09,655
I'll be too busy to go.

752
00:43:10,325 --> 00:43:13,025
The defendant treated the plaintiff as more than a business partner...

753
00:43:13,825 --> 00:43:16,165
and made every effort to maintain an amicable relationship.

754
00:43:16,665 --> 00:43:17,665
What do you think, CEO Baek?

755
00:43:17,735 --> 00:43:20,465
The last time I went shopping was, what, four? Five years ago?

756
00:43:20,665 --> 00:43:22,565
But my wife does it every week. Every single week.

757
00:43:23,435 --> 00:43:24,875
She gets ten packages a day.

758
00:43:28,175 --> 00:43:29,645
Even when the plaintiff purchased...

759
00:43:29,705 --> 00:43:31,575
expensive luxury bags she could not afford,

760
00:43:32,215 --> 00:43:34,545
the defendant considered it part of maintaining her image as CEO...

761
00:43:35,815 --> 00:43:36,985
and acquiesced.

762
00:43:39,515 --> 00:43:42,685
The defendant has never assaulted the plaintiff.

763
00:43:43,855 --> 00:43:45,225
Rather, the plaintiff, who was intoxicated...

764
00:43:45,295 --> 00:43:46,295
due to work-related stress,

765
00:43:46,295 --> 00:43:48,095
caused a disturbance with a kitchen knife,

766
00:43:49,865 --> 00:43:51,495
placing the defendant in danger.

767
00:43:52,135 --> 00:43:53,765
The injuries claimed by the plaintiff...

768
00:43:54,235 --> 00:43:56,565
were sustained as the defendant was trying to restrain her...

769
00:43:56,935 --> 00:43:58,575
and were therefore unavoidable.

770
00:43:59,035 --> 00:44:00,905
- And about refusing intimacy... - The one who unilaterally...

771
00:44:00,905 --> 00:44:02,345
refused intimacy...

772
00:44:02,845 --> 00:44:04,445
was the plaintiff, not the defendant.

773
00:44:05,445 --> 00:44:06,545
The plaintiff was the first...

774
00:44:06,615 --> 00:44:08,185
to suggest sleeping in separate rooms.

775
00:44:09,845 --> 00:44:11,955
Afterward, they were both preoccupied with their work,

776
00:44:12,815 --> 00:44:15,025
and naturally grew distant,

777
00:44:16,125 --> 00:44:18,255
so this cannot be the defendant's sole responsibility.

778
00:44:19,155 --> 00:44:21,665
The defendant is making efforts to restore the marriage.

779
00:44:22,665 --> 00:44:25,265
The defendant does not wish to dissolve this marriage.

780
00:44:26,135 --> 00:44:28,265
He earnestly hopes that the plaintiff...

781
00:44:29,605 --> 00:44:31,335
will give him the opportunity to actively...

782
00:44:31,575 --> 00:44:33,305
recommit to their relationship.

783
00:44:34,075 --> 00:44:35,545
Does this make any sense?

784
00:44:36,075 --> 00:44:38,545
How can he be so shameless?

785
00:44:39,145 --> 00:44:41,485
After how he treated me throughout our entire marriage.

786
00:44:42,015 --> 00:44:44,615
That's standard procedure in these documents.

787
00:44:45,085 --> 00:44:46,085
And I told you.

788
00:44:46,155 --> 00:44:48,325
That's not your husband. It's that 200-year-old...

789
00:44:51,095 --> 00:44:53,125
That's a tactic from his lawyer.

790
00:44:54,225 --> 00:44:55,465
Leaving everything else aside,

791
00:44:56,295 --> 00:44:57,295
it's this part.

792
00:44:57,525 --> 00:45:00,265
The part where it says I caused a disturbance with a kitchen knife.

793
00:45:03,865 --> 00:45:05,435
I may have caused the disturbance,

794
00:45:06,705 --> 00:45:10,205
but I was the only one who got hurt because of it.

795
00:45:13,275 --> 00:45:14,275
Is that so?

796
00:45:15,115 --> 00:45:16,245
In that case,

797
00:45:16,245 --> 00:45:20,185
could you describe that incident in more detail?

798
00:45:27,865 --> 00:45:28,925
That day,

799
00:45:32,395 --> 00:45:33,465
I was alone,

800
00:45:35,565 --> 00:45:36,565
collapsed...

801
00:45:38,105 --> 00:45:40,075
on the floor for a long time.

802
00:45:46,045 --> 00:45:47,075
He just left me...

803
00:45:48,985 --> 00:45:50,915
on that cold floor...

804
00:45:56,485 --> 00:46:00,095
My husband had abandoned me again...

805
00:46:04,795 --> 00:46:07,595
at my most vulnerable moment.

806
00:46:24,015 --> 00:46:25,015
(Won Ho)

807
00:46:25,555 --> 00:46:28,155
I had to see Father Kwon, so I left early.

808
00:46:28,985 --> 00:46:30,685
Wash up and make sure you eat something.

809
00:46:48,745 --> 00:46:51,445
Twice, for the same reason...

810
00:47:03,825 --> 00:47:04,825
That's enough.

811
00:47:06,795 --> 00:47:08,995
I think we've won.

812
00:47:18,275 --> 00:47:20,335
- Welcome. Right this way, please. - Welcome.

813
00:47:20,975 --> 00:47:23,745
- Welcome. Yes, this way, please. - This way.

814
00:47:23,845 --> 00:47:24,845
Welcome.

815
00:47:24,915 --> 00:47:26,375
And about this, from earlier...

816
00:47:26,445 --> 00:47:29,485
For the men's outfits, you can start by picking a colour.

817
00:47:29,545 --> 00:47:30,545
For the wedding dress,

818
00:47:30,545 --> 00:47:31,615
let's go with this off-the-shoulder one...

819
00:47:31,785 --> 00:47:33,185
Okay, got it.

820
00:47:34,355 --> 00:47:35,355
Length is...

821
00:47:36,985 --> 00:47:37,995
Yes.

822
00:47:38,895 --> 00:47:40,855
Arm length is half...

823
00:47:41,695 --> 00:47:42,695
There.

824
00:48:06,285 --> 00:48:09,555
It's really packed in here.

825
00:48:10,355 --> 00:48:13,495
It looks like each couple brought five or six family members.

826
00:48:14,025 --> 00:48:15,995
Sons-in-law, daughters-in-law, grandchildren...

827
00:48:16,695 --> 00:48:19,265
One family even brought their in-laws.

828
00:48:19,565 --> 00:48:23,165
This isn't just a wedding, it's a full-on festival.

829
00:48:23,965 --> 00:48:24,975
Tell me about it.

830
00:48:25,235 --> 00:48:28,145
If I'd known, I would've prepared some food for a feast.

831
00:48:28,305 --> 00:48:29,345
Maybe we should have?

832
00:48:35,315 --> 00:48:36,885
You look absolutely stunning.

833
00:48:57,265 --> 00:48:58,405
You're here.

834
00:48:59,205 --> 00:49:01,475
I saw on the way in. You've really prepared a lot.

835
00:49:02,075 --> 00:49:04,175
- You're a true professional. - It's just the basics.

836
00:49:05,645 --> 00:49:07,715
Are you feeling better now?

837
00:49:08,815 --> 00:49:09,815
Yes.

838
00:49:13,185 --> 00:49:14,825
It feels like you have a slight fever, though.

839
00:49:15,825 --> 00:49:16,985
No, I'm fine.

840
00:49:17,555 --> 00:49:18,825
Don't push yourself too hard.

841
00:49:20,355 --> 00:49:21,365
Take this when you feel tired.

842
00:49:23,395 --> 00:49:24,395
Thanks.

843
00:49:33,975 --> 00:49:35,845
(Energy Care Up)

844
00:49:41,685 --> 00:49:42,785
Shall we go, then?

845
00:49:43,815 --> 00:49:44,815
Yes.

846
00:49:51,795 --> 00:49:55,095
You look so beautiful. Really. Could you move a little closer?

847
00:49:55,165 --> 00:49:56,565
Yes, that's great.

848
00:50:04,705 --> 00:50:05,705
How's it going?

849
00:50:06,005 --> 00:50:07,005
You're here.

850
00:50:07,705 --> 00:50:08,705
So, what do you think?

851
00:50:09,005 --> 00:50:11,075
Doesn't it make you want to get married too?

852
00:50:11,145 --> 00:50:12,245
You little rascal.

853
00:50:21,885 --> 00:50:23,155
Yes, keep smiling.

854
00:50:23,755 --> 00:50:26,855
Gosh, seeing you here is something else.

855
00:50:27,125 --> 00:50:29,095
You're different from the brides I usually see.

856
00:50:29,165 --> 00:50:30,165
How so?

857
00:50:30,225 --> 00:50:33,065
Among all the brides here today, how would I rank in terms of looks?

858
00:50:34,165 --> 00:50:35,665
Well, you're not in last place.

859
00:50:38,775 --> 00:50:40,505
My friend said he was having a vow renewal,

860
00:50:40,575 --> 00:50:41,575
so I wanted to see you...

861
00:50:41,645 --> 00:50:43,375
and check things out while I was at it.

862
00:50:43,975 --> 00:50:45,345
But I actually feel proud.

863
00:50:46,615 --> 00:50:48,245
Wearing a dress at our age...

864
00:50:48,645 --> 00:50:50,115
is honestly something we can't even dream of.

865
00:50:50,845 --> 00:50:52,955
You're really doing something amazing.

866
00:50:53,285 --> 00:50:55,925
Come on, it's not like I'm doing volunteer work.

867
00:50:56,755 --> 00:50:58,055
At our community center,

868
00:50:58,955 --> 00:51:01,525
there are many elderly people who still haven't had a wedding.

869
00:51:01,725 --> 00:51:02,725
Really?

870
00:51:03,025 --> 00:51:04,995
They still haven't had a wedding ceremony?

871
00:51:05,165 --> 00:51:06,165
A lot of them.

872
00:51:06,495 --> 00:51:09,065
This isn't something everyone gets to enjoy.

873
00:51:09,705 --> 00:51:11,105
Then I'll do it for them.

874
00:51:11,365 --> 00:51:14,005
- What? - The vow renewal for the seniors.

875
00:51:14,435 --> 00:51:15,445
I'll do it.

876
00:51:16,375 --> 00:51:19,175
Why is this coming up all of a sudden?

877
00:51:19,445 --> 00:51:20,445
More volunteer work?

878
00:51:21,215 --> 00:51:23,115
Come on, it's not "more."

879
00:51:23,385 --> 00:51:25,485
This is my first time volunteering for a vow renewal.

880
00:51:25,615 --> 00:51:28,385
Be serious. What are you thinking?

881
00:51:28,585 --> 00:51:30,425
Today's the first day of the event.

882
00:51:30,525 --> 00:51:31,855
Do you have to bring that up right now?

883
00:51:31,925 --> 00:51:33,025
Can't you see how busy I am?

884
00:51:33,895 --> 00:51:35,195
I know, but...

885
00:51:35,395 --> 00:51:36,925
I was talking to Father Kwon,

886
00:51:36,995 --> 00:51:39,295
and I'm telling you now before I forget.

887
00:51:39,895 --> 00:51:40,895
What?

888
00:51:41,565 --> 00:51:42,565
Who did you say?

889
00:51:42,935 --> 00:51:44,875
Father Kwon stopped by earlier.

890
00:51:45,575 --> 00:51:47,405
He came to support his friend's wedding.

891
00:51:50,645 --> 00:51:54,675
Ji Won Ho. You are truly hopeless.

892
00:51:56,615 --> 00:52:01,085
Have you forgotten why we're exchanging these complaints?

893
00:52:02,325 --> 00:52:04,425
It's all because of your precious Father Kwon.

894
00:52:04,525 --> 00:52:06,725
What happened to Dallae was because of him.

895
00:52:06,825 --> 00:52:08,095
Watch your mouth.

896
00:52:08,765 --> 00:52:11,125
How is that Father Kwon's fault? It's our fault.

897
00:52:12,595 --> 00:52:14,195
You keep bringing up old wounds...

898
00:52:14,265 --> 00:52:16,935
and blaming others. Break that awful habit, please.

899
00:52:24,045 --> 00:52:26,845
Why don't you just shut up?

900
00:52:56,845 --> 00:52:57,845
Mi Young.

901
00:53:02,145 --> 00:53:03,145
It's been a while.

902
00:53:06,155 --> 00:53:07,315
I didn't mean to,

903
00:53:07,715 --> 00:53:09,855
but I overheard you and Won Ho earlier.

904
00:53:11,525 --> 00:53:12,695
About that day...

905
00:53:13,695 --> 00:53:14,925
I'm sorry, Mi Young.

906
00:53:17,895 --> 00:53:19,335
If you were truly sorry,

907
00:53:21,565 --> 00:53:22,865
you wouldn't be here.

908
00:53:25,805 --> 00:53:26,805
For me,

909
00:53:27,375 --> 00:53:29,475
it's painful just to see you.

910
00:53:31,405 --> 00:53:32,415
I understand.

911
00:53:34,275 --> 00:53:36,415
Then, goodbye.

912
00:53:38,015 --> 00:53:39,185
Won Ho was hurting too.

913
00:53:42,625 --> 00:53:44,655
For a long time, he was hurting...

914
00:53:45,455 --> 00:53:46,455
just as much as you were.

915
00:53:46,555 --> 00:53:48,395
Hurting how? How?

916
00:53:49,665 --> 00:53:51,095
The truth is, that day...

917
00:55:06,935 --> 00:55:08,975
That's the last time I'm ever mentioning volunteering.

918
00:55:34,995 --> 00:55:36,005
I...

919
00:55:38,305 --> 00:55:39,375
have something to say.

920
00:55:39,835 --> 00:55:40,835
What is it now?

921
00:55:40,905 --> 00:55:42,675
Are you going to slap my other cheek this time?

922
00:55:44,305 --> 00:55:45,345
I just...

923
00:55:48,375 --> 00:55:50,615
finished talking with Father Kwon.

924
00:55:55,585 --> 00:55:57,625
What about?

925
00:56:00,225 --> 00:56:01,555
About that day.

926
00:56:08,765 --> 00:56:11,465
I know it was a favour for Father Kwon, but still...

927
00:56:11,535 --> 00:56:13,235
Can't you see all this work piled up?

928
00:56:13,705 --> 00:56:15,845
We're on a tight deadline even with both of us.

929
00:56:16,705 --> 00:56:19,675
Are you really going to dump it all on me and leave?

930
00:56:20,715 --> 00:56:23,015
I know it'll be hard on you by yourself.

931
00:56:23,385 --> 00:56:24,685
But Father Kwon...

932
00:56:24,945 --> 00:56:26,885
is like a father to me.

933
00:56:27,285 --> 00:56:29,225
How could I turn down his request?

934
00:56:30,285 --> 00:56:31,285
That day,

935
00:56:32,395 --> 00:56:34,125
you were going to come back, right?

936
00:56:40,465 --> 00:56:42,405
Yes, Father Kwon. I'm on my way now.

937
00:56:42,765 --> 00:56:43,935
Oh, what should I do?

938
00:56:44,235 --> 00:56:45,435
I'm so worried about Mi Young,

939
00:56:45,505 --> 00:56:47,605
I think I have to turn the car around.

940
00:56:47,935 --> 00:56:49,805
I'll send a friend over right away instead.

941
00:56:49,905 --> 00:56:52,475
I'm sorry, Father. I'll call you back.

942
00:56:55,585 --> 00:56:56,645
Darn it.

943
00:57:05,495 --> 00:57:08,095
- Trying to get someone killed? - Are you all right?

944
00:57:08,155 --> 00:57:10,595
You think I would be? Would you be all right?

945
00:57:10,665 --> 00:57:11,965
- What will you do? - Please call your insurance.

946
00:57:12,035 --> 00:57:13,035
Insurance?

947
00:57:13,095 --> 00:57:14,395
Look, I'm short on time, so let's call the insurance...

948
00:57:14,465 --> 00:57:15,465
I don't have time either.

949
00:57:16,735 --> 00:57:19,835
(Mi Young)

950
00:57:20,235 --> 00:57:21,435
I don't think it was an illegal U-turn.

951
00:57:21,505 --> 00:57:22,905
He's been drinking, if you ask me. He's drunk.

952
00:57:22,975 --> 00:57:23,975
Hey, say something.

953
00:57:24,045 --> 00:57:25,515
Just a moment. Let me just make one phone call.

954
00:57:25,575 --> 00:57:27,015
I'm telling you, he was drinking.

955
00:57:37,685 --> 00:57:39,395
Wait, what's this all of a sudden?

956
00:57:39,895 --> 00:57:41,255
Why are you bringing that up now?

957
00:57:43,065 --> 00:57:44,065
And...

958
00:57:47,065 --> 00:57:48,935
the day I tried to kill myself.

959
00:57:53,005 --> 00:57:54,005
That day too,

960
00:57:56,005 --> 00:57:57,745
you didn't abandon me.

961
00:58:00,015 --> 00:58:01,515
I begged you not to leave.

962
00:58:02,545 --> 00:58:04,215
I told you I couldn't be alone.

963
00:58:05,215 --> 00:58:06,715
I begged you not to go.

964
00:58:07,355 --> 00:58:10,355
I pleaded with you that I couldn't handle it alone.

965
00:58:11,025 --> 00:58:13,255
You're right. I'm sorry for everything.

966
00:58:13,555 --> 00:58:15,095
It's all my fault. I'm so sorry.

967
00:58:15,825 --> 00:58:17,795
I'm a complete wreck.

968
00:58:19,095 --> 00:58:20,665
My mom and dad are gone,

969
00:58:21,365 --> 00:58:22,605
and Dallae is gone too.

970
00:58:23,905 --> 00:58:25,805
I couldn't even protect my own child.

971
00:58:26,775 --> 00:58:29,475
I want to be gone too.

972
00:58:30,805 --> 00:58:34,615
- I want to be gone too. - No, why would you think that?

973
00:58:34,675 --> 00:58:36,285
Don't say that, Mi Young.

974
00:58:36,685 --> 00:58:37,685
Let go.

975
00:58:42,385 --> 00:58:43,455
Stay away.

976
00:58:43,525 --> 00:58:46,655
I'm going to die. I want to die.

977
00:58:46,825 --> 00:58:48,665
Mi Young, first, put that down, okay?

978
00:58:49,065 --> 00:58:50,065
Put it down.

979
00:58:50,125 --> 00:58:52,195
Stay away. Don't come any closer.

980
00:58:52,195 --> 00:58:53,195
Put it down.

981
00:58:53,265 --> 00:58:54,335
No.

982
00:58:58,605 --> 00:58:59,875
Don't!

983
00:59:00,335 --> 00:59:01,335
Darn it.

984
00:59:02,005 --> 00:59:04,705
- Baek Mi Young, snap out of it. - Don't.

985
00:59:04,775 --> 00:59:09,085
I said don't. I want to die.

986
00:59:09,445 --> 00:59:10,985
The one who almost died that day...

987
00:59:12,885 --> 00:59:14,085
wasn't me.

988
00:59:18,085 --> 00:59:19,125
Hey, Baek Mi Young!

989
00:59:37,075 --> 00:59:39,515
I want to die so badly.

990
00:59:45,655 --> 00:59:48,085
I want to die...

991
00:59:53,125 --> 00:59:54,395
The one who got stabbed...

992
00:59:57,195 --> 00:59:58,195
was you.

993
00:59:59,735 --> 01:00:01,365
What are you talking about? I have to work.

994
01:00:01,435 --> 01:00:02,435
Get out.

995
01:00:05,375 --> 01:00:06,535
No, Mi Young, wait.

996
01:00:06,705 --> 01:00:07,935
No, wait.

997
01:00:08,005 --> 01:00:09,045
Mi Young, just wait.

998
01:00:26,695 --> 01:00:27,795
It wasn't you.

999
01:00:29,995 --> 01:00:30,995
It was me.

1000
01:00:36,535 --> 01:00:38,775
I was the one who put you in danger.

1001
01:00:41,235 --> 01:00:42,245
I...

1002
01:00:43,145 --> 01:00:45,205
I almost killed you.

1003
01:00:47,415 --> 01:00:49,085
I'm sorry.

1004
01:00:50,345 --> 01:00:51,445
I'm sorry.

1005
01:00:52,615 --> 01:00:53,685
I'm sorry.

1006
01:01:00,725 --> 01:01:01,855
What do I do?

1007
01:01:25,015 --> 01:01:27,985
(OK! Let's Get Divorced)

1008
01:01:28,785 --> 01:01:31,855
You want me to pretend I don't know? You think this feels natural?

1009
01:01:31,925 --> 01:01:32,925
Let's just do it, honey.

1010
01:01:33,225 --> 01:01:34,755
Do it? Wait, honey?

1011
01:01:34,755 --> 01:01:36,065
What's with you two?

1012
01:01:36,295 --> 01:01:38,295
You're being so uncomfortably nice to him...

1013
01:01:38,365 --> 01:01:40,135
to make Won Ho leave on his own accord...

1014
01:01:40,195 --> 01:01:41,195
Lawsuit strategy?

1015
01:01:41,735 --> 01:01:44,105
Just act normal, please.

1016
01:01:44,505 --> 01:01:46,235
Gosh, you're really going to be like this to the end.

1017
01:01:46,305 --> 01:01:49,105
- You're such a stubborn leech. - Yes, I'm a stubborn leech.

1018
01:01:49,175 --> 01:01:50,205
But you're just pigheaded.

1019
01:01:50,275 --> 01:01:52,515
Are you trying to wreck a home?

1020
01:01:52,775 --> 01:01:54,915
Do you think my son is crazy to date a girl like you?

1021
01:01:54,975 --> 01:01:56,315
That's right. I am crazy.

1022
01:01:56,385 --> 01:01:57,385
I am...

1023
01:01:57,685 --> 01:01:58,685
Ahn Hee Ju's...

1024
01:01:59,785 --> 01:02:00,785
boyfriend.

